WEBVTT

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.800
Vector, open up!

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.880
First give me the moon.
Then we'll talk.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.280
- Mr Gru!
- Zip it, Happy Meal.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.800
Now, the girls.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.080
Actually, I think I'll hold on to
them a little while longer.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.160
No!

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.800
Oh, yeah! Unpredictable!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.880
Listen close, you little punk.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.200
When I get in there,
you are in for a world of pain!

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.200
I'm really scared!

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.280
He is gonna kick your butt.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.720
What? He punched my shark!

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.440
There he is!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.320
Hang on, Gru.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.680
Oh, no!

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.320
Vector has the girls. Go!

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.760
What happened to the ship?
It's big again!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.600
- Not as big as the moon is going
to be! - What?

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.520
The larger the mass of an object,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.400
the quicker the effects
of the shrink ray wear off!

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.320
I call it the Nefario Principle.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.240
I just came up with it now,
actually.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.480
Oh, no!

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.560
Did you see that?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.280
- Vector! Help!
- Vector!

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.520
- Over here!
- Hey!

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.160
What are you girls
doing back there?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.240
The moon!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.720
Watch out!

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.120
Get as close in as you can.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.160
You got it.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.960
- Mr Gru, up here!
- Mr Gru!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.000
Okay, girls! Girls!

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.680
- You're going to have to jump.
- Jump?

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.600
Are you insane?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.040
Don't worry, I will catch you.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.280
You gave us back!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.360
I know, I know. And it is
the worst mistake I ever made.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.760
But you have to jump now.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.320
It'll be okay.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.080
Okay, girls.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.520
Jump now!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.520
Margo, I will catch you.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.080
And I will never let you go again.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.240
- Not so fast!
- No!

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.520
Let me go!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.360
Margo!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.040
I'm coming, Margo. Hang on!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.240
I got you.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.720
No!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.400
Oh, poop.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:02.200
This time, good triumphs,

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.280
and the moon has been returned
to its rightful place in the sky.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.840
But once again, law enforcement
is baffled,

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.080
leaving everyone to wonder,

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.880
who is this mysterious hero?

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.840
And what will he do next?

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.080
Okay, girls. Time for bed.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.720
- Come on! We want a story.
- Three sleepy kittens!

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.880
Oh, no! Sorry. That book was
accidentally destroyed maliciously.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.320
Tonight we are going
to read a new book.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.520
This one is called

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.120
One Big Unicorn by...
Who wrote this?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.440
Me! I wrote it.
Look, it's a puppet book!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.840
Here, watch this.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.720
That's the horn!

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.560
This is gonna be
the best book ever!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:54.240
Not to pat myself on the back,
but, yes, it probably will be.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.360
Here we go.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.320
"One big unicorn, strong and free

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.000
"thought he was happy
as he could be.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.600
"Then three little kittens
came around

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:09.520
"and turned his whole life
upside down."

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.280
Hey, that one looks like me!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.400
No, what are you talking about?
These are kittens!

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:17.080
Any relation to persons living or
dead is completely coincidental.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.760
"They made him laugh.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.960
"They made him cry.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.480
"He never should have said goodbye.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.680
"And now he knows
he could never part

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.240
"from those three little kittens

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.520
"that changed his heart.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.600
"The end."

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.880
Okay, all right. Good night.

